# Humility's "lose all abilities" is a layer-6 effect with Humility's timestamp (CR 613.1f, 613.7): it takes the
# abilities granted before it and leaves those granted after. Bot1's first Llanowar Elves gets Rancor ("Enchanted
# creature gets +2/+0 and has trample") on turn 1, before Humility (turn 3): it loses that trample. The second Elves and
# its Rancor come on turn 5, after Humility: that Rancor's timestamp is later (CR 613.7d, 613.7e), so that Elves keeps
# trample. Both are 3/1 - Humility's base 1/1, then Rancor's +2/+0 in layer 7c, which is Rancor's ability, not the
# creature's, and applies either way.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Plains
Mox Emerald
Mox Pearl
Llanowar Elves
Rancor
Rancor
Humility
Llanowar Elves
Forest x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

